We are given the system of equations
\begin{align*} 5u &= -7 - 2v \\ 3u &= 4v - 25 \end{align*}
We want to find an ordered pair $(u,v)$ that solves the system.
From the first equation, we can write $2v = -5u - 7$, so $v = -\frac{5}{2}u - \frac{7}{2}$.
Substituting this into the second equation, we have
\begin{align*} 3u &= 4 \left( -\frac{5}{2} u - \frac{7}{2} \right) - 25 \\ 3u &= -10u - 14 - 25 \\ 3u &= -10u - 39 \\ 13u &= -39 \\ u &= -3 \end{align*}
Then
\begin{align*} v &= -\frac{5}{2} (-3) - \frac{7}{2} \\ &= \frac{15}{2} - \frac{7}{2} \\ &= \frac{8}{2} \\ &= 4 \end{align*}
Thus, $(u,v) = (-3, 4)$.
