Let $c = \cos \theta.$ We are given that $c = \frac{1}{3}.$ We want to find $\cos 5 \theta.$
We have the following identities:
\begin{align*} \cos 2 \theta &= 2 \cos^2 \theta - 1 = 2c^2 - 1 \\ \cos 3 \theta &= 4 \cos^3 \theta - 3 \cos \theta = 4c^3 - 3c \\ \cos 4 \theta &= 2 \cos^2 2 \theta - 1 = 2 (2c^2 - 1)^2 - 1 = 2 (4c^4 - 4c^2 + 1) - 1 = 8c^4 - 8c^2 + 1 \\ \cos 5 \theta &= \cos (3 \theta + 2 \theta) = \cos 3 \theta \cos 2 \theta - \sin 3 \theta \sin 2 \theta \end{align*}
Also,
\begin{align*} \cos 5 \theta &= 16 \cos^5 \theta - 20 \cos^3 \theta + 5 \cos \theta \\ &= 16c^5 - 20c^3 + 5c \end{align*}
Then
\begin{align*} \cos 5 \theta &= 16 \left( \frac{1}{3} \right)^5 - 20 \left( \frac{1}{3} \right)^3 + 5 \left( \frac{1}{3} \right) \\ &= 16 \left( \frac{1}{243} \right) - 20 \left( \frac{1}{27} \right) + \frac{5}{3} \\ &= \frac{16}{243} - \frac{20}{27} + \frac{5}{3} \\ &= \frac{16}{243} - \frac{180}{243} + \frac{405}{243} \\ &= \frac{16 - 180 + 405}{243} \\ &= \frac{241}{243} \end{align*}

Thus, $\cos 5 \theta = 16 \cos^5 \theta - 20 \cos^3 \theta + 5 \cos \theta.$
We have $\cos \theta = \frac{1}{3}.$ Then
\begin{align*} \cos 5 \theta &= 16 \left( \frac{1}{3} \right)^5 - 20 \left( \frac{1}{3} \right)^3 + 5 \left( \frac{1}{3} \right) \\ &= 16 \cdot \frac{1}{243} - 20 \cdot \frac{1}{27} + 5 \cdot \frac{1}{3} \\ &= \frac{16}{243} - \frac{20}{27} + \frac{5}{3} \\ &= \frac{16}{243} - \frac{180}{243} + \frac{405}{243} \\ &= \frac{16 - 180 + 405}{243} \\ &= \frac{241}{243} \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{\frac{241}{243}}$

