Let $P(x) = 2x^3 - 3x^2 + 165x - 4$. Since $a, b, c$ are the roots of the polynomial $P(x)$, we have
\begin{align*} a+b+c &= \frac{-(-3)}{2} = \frac{3}{2} \\ ab+bc+ca &= \frac{165}{2} \\ abc &= \frac{-(-4)}{2} = 2 \end{align*}
Let $x = a+b-1$, $y = b+c-1$, and $z = c+a-1$. Then we want to compute $x^3 + y^3 + z^3$.

We have
\begin{align*} x+y+z &= (a+b-1) + (b+c-1) + (c+a-1) \\ &= 2(a+b+c) - 3 \\ &= 2\left(\frac{3}{2}\right) - 3 \\ &= 3-3 = 0 \end{align*}
Since $x+y+z = 0$, we have $x^3+y^3+z^3 = 3xyz$.
Thus, we want to compute $3(a+b-1)(b+c-1)(c+a-1)$.

\begin{align*} a+b-1 &= a+b+c - c - 1 = \frac{3}{2} - c - 1 = \frac{1}{2} - c \\ b+c-1 &= a+b+c - a - 1 = \frac{3}{2} - a - 1 = \frac{1}{2} - a \\ c+a-1 &= a+b+c - b - 1 = \frac{3}{2} - b - 1 = \frac{1}{2} - b \end{align*}
So we want to compute $3\left(\frac{1}{2} - a\right)\left(\frac{1}{2} - b\right)\left(\frac{1}{2} - c\right)$.
\begin{align*} 3\left(\frac{1}{2} - a\right)\left(\frac{1}{2} - b\right)\left(\frac{1}{2} - c\right) &= 3\left[ \left(\frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{2}a - \frac{1}{2}b + ab\right)\left(\frac{1}{2} - c\right) \right] \\ &= 3\left[ \frac{1}{8} - \frac{1}{4}a - \frac{1}{4}b + \frac{1}{2}ab - \frac{1}{4}c + \frac{1}{2}ac + \frac{1}{2}bc - abc \right] \\ &= 3\left[ \frac{1}{8} - \frac{1}{4}(a+b+c) + \frac{1}{2}(ab+bc+ca) - abc \right] \\ &= 3\left[ \frac{1}{8} - \frac{1}{4}\left(\frac{3}{2}\right) + \frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{165}{2}\right) - 2 \right] \\ &= 3\left[ \frac{1}{8} - \frac{3}{8} + \frac{165}{4} - 2 \right] \\ &= 3\left[ -\frac{2}{8} + \frac{165}{4} - \frac{8}{4} \right] \\ &= 3\left[ -\frac{1}{4} + \frac{157}{4} \right] \\ &= 3\left[ \frac{156}{4} \right] \\ &= 3(39) = 117 \end{align*}
Thus, $(a+b-1)^3 + (b+c-1)^3 + (c+a-1)^3 = 117$.

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{117}$

