solution.answer:
Let $\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}.$  Then the area of the parallelogram generated by $\mathbf{v}$ and $\mathbf{w}$ is
\begin{align*} \|\mathbf{v} \times \mathbf{w}\| &= \left\| \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} \times \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \right\| \\ &= \left\| \begin{pmatrix} (1)(4) - (-2)(-3) \\ (-2)(1) - (3)(4) \\ (3)(-3) - (1)(1) \end{pmatrix} \right\| \\ &= \left\| \begin{pmatrix} 4 - 6 \\ -2 - 12 \\ -9 - 1 \end{pmatrix} \right\| \\ &= \left\| \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -14 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix} \right\| \\ &= \sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2} \\ &= \sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} \\ &= \sqrt{300} \\ &= \sqrt{100 \cdot 3} \\ &= 10 \sqrt{3}. \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{10 \sqrt{3}}$

